<div class="inline-confirm" role="alert">
  <span>{{message}}</span>
  <div class="inline-confirm__actions">
    <form method="POST" action="{{confirmAction}}">
      <button type="submit" class="btn-small btn-danger"
        {{#if htmxPost}}hx-post="{{htmxPost}}" hx-target="{{htmxTarget}}" hx-swap="{{htmxSwap}}"{{/if}}>Confirm</button>
    </form>
    <button type="button" class="btn-small" data-confirm-cancel>Cancel</button>
  </div>
  {{!-- cancelHtml is server-built, trusted markup (fixed template + validated, encodeURIComponent'd IDs). It is kept inert in a <template> and restored via cloneNode in admin.js — never parsed from a string at runtime — so it is not an XSS sink. Do not feed user-controlled data into cancelHtml. --}}
  <template data-cancel-restore>{{{cancelHtml}}}</template>
</div>